From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Austin Shirley <austin@deadband.dev>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:30:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(st): make BL33_CFG optional

Only add the HW_CONFIG payload when BL33_CFG is set. BL33 then uses
its own DT, e.g. U-Boot with its appended DT, which is then covered
by the BL33 hash.

Resolves failed builds caused by fiptool always taking the next option
as the HW_CONFIG file when BL33_CFG is unset.

Tested on STM32MP135.

Change-Id: Ic588cc7d580b20b1c3f3734b716190e6955d88f7
Upstream: https://github.com/TrustedFirmware-A/trusted-firmware-a/commit/57ea6e29d64a27e5f969802a14a366ce93863b2e
Signed-off-by: Austin Shirley <austin@deadband.dev>
---

diff --git a/docs/plat/st/stm32mpus.rst b/docs/plat/st/stm32mpus.rst
index 995ae81..7e8ad3b 100644
--- a/docs/plat/st/stm32mpus.rst
+++ b/docs/plat/st/stm32mpus.rst
@@ -51,6 +51,11 @@
 
 Other configuration flags:
 
+- | ``BL33_CFG``: optional HW_CONFIG device-tree blob, added to the FIP.
+  | When unset, BL33 uses its own embedded DT (e.g. ``u-boot.bin``, U-Boot with
+  | its appended DT), which is then covered by the BL33 hash. The ``hw-config``
+  | node must then be removed from the board FW_CONFIG.
+  | Default: unset
 - | ``DTB_FILE_NAME``: to precise board device-tree blob to be used.
   | Default: stm32mp157c-ev1.dtb
 - | ``DWL_BUFFER_BASE``: the 'serial boot' load address of FIP,
diff --git a/plat/st/common/common.mk b/plat/st/common/common.mk
index d32f831..f4b71f7 100644
--- a/plat/st/common/common.mk
+++ b/plat/st/common/common.mk
@@ -122,10 +122,13 @@
 STM32_DEPS			+=	${STM32IMAGE}
 
 FIP_DEPS			+=	dtbs
-STM32MP_HW_CONFIG		:=	${BL33_CFG}
 
-# Add the HW_CONFIG to FIP and specify the same to certtool
+# BL33_CFG is optional: without it, BL33 uses its own embedded DT.
+ifneq (${BL33_CFG},)
+STM32MP_HW_CONFIG		:=	${BL33_CFG}
+# Add the HW_CONFIG to FIP and specify the same to certtool.
 $(eval $(call TOOL_ADD_PAYLOAD,${STM32MP_HW_CONFIG},--hw-config))
+endif
 
 # Add the build options to pack Trusted OS Extra1 and Trusted OS Extra2 images
 # in the FIP if the platform requires.
